  "caption": "Quinn's plan for a sore ankle: ignore it. Six weeks later, still sore, plus a shoulder niggle back for the third time this year.\n\nA rough guide: everyday strains and flare-ups without warning signs can get one to two weeks of sensible self-care. If it isn't clearly improving by then, book an assessment.\n\nSelf-care that often helps: keep moving but ease off the trigger, protect your sleep, and use heat or ice for comfort. Book sooner if pain wakes you, keeps returning, changes how you move, or comes with tingling.\n\nCan't bear weight, spreading numbness, or new bladder or bowel changes? Seek same-day medical care.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
